# _Active — what now

Current priorities, seeded from [[STRATEGY]]'s bottleneck + the [[MOC - v1]] checklist. Frequently updated.

## Operating model — Claude plans, Codex executes

**Claude = planner/reviewer; Codex = executor.** For the four-app v1 push, Codex is executing the written per-app EXECUTE blocks directly in isolated worktrees; the start-orchestration bootstrap remains suspended until the repos are in known state. Claude still provides independent A5 review/approval before merge/deploy. Full handoff + recon + open decisions: [[2026-06-01 1815 — Four-app v1 plan + Codex execution handoff]]. Detailed per-app checklist: [[MOC - v1 Verification Steps]]. Cross-app context source: [[Four-app v1 control ledger]].

**Autonomous = additive / reversible / observable** (STRATEGY's guardrail). A gate = destructive, irreversible, external-facing, or a judgment call.

**Browser V1 acceptance gate:** fixture seeding, SQL assertions, unit/integration tests, GitHub Actions, and Playwright automation are scaffolding/supporting evidence only. Browser V1 is not accepted until Chrome/Chrome DevTools real-browser execution proves the persona flows through visible UI outcomes, screenshots, console/network inspection where relevant, and browser-console probes where required. Do not use Codex in-app browser / MAP / `iab` as the acceptance surface unless Jarrad explicitly reverses this.

**Browser V1 UI-created data rule:** data setup is part of the browser test. For [[Closer Lab]] and [[BMH Institute]], create fixture/content/test records through Chrome/DevTools browser UI wherever the app UI supports creation or editing. Direct database/API writes are exception-only supporting setup for things the UI cannot create, such as auth bootstrap when no signup/admin UI exists, and must be labeled as non-acceptance evidence.

**2026-06-02 browser-surface correction:** Jarrad first reset [[Closer Lab]] and [[BMH Institute]] Browser V1 acceptance to zero, then superseded the MAP/in-app-browser requirement with Chrome/DevTools real-browser execution. Current controller evidence shows [[BMH Institute]] residual proof closed and [[Closer Lab]] Browser V1 markers closed for pre-read persistence, signed embed-token proof, and scoring/runtime. [[Sandra]] production-readiness proof is GO as of 2026-06-11. The 2026-06-18 active-front reset (skip-trace/CASS preflight, filter preset discoverability, bulk tag creation, Sendillo-era Overview KPI visibility) is now CLEARED 2026-06-19 — all four shipped via merged PRs #288–#300, plus Messages disposition/outcomes hardening (#298/#299/#300). Remaining [[Sandra]] threads: PR #287 (hide dead-dispositioned leads from the kanban — OPEN, awaiting NULL-handling review) and the bulk-SMS→Campaigns KPI tracking gap (June 19 run, job `72b0e08d`, 7,547 messages queued with `campaignId=null`) — forward fix now tracked under **PR #306** (supersedes #301; per the 2026-06-23 [[Sandra PR 306 merge gate rules]] decision, updated 2026-07-05 — merge via GitHub-backed main once the Playwright golden-paths check passes; PR MERGEABLE/UNSTABLE, **not yet merged**) which requires a campaign name + auto-creates + stamps `campaign_id`, with the 2026-06-19 architect P1s folded in; the **June 19 backfill is still pending** (designed, not applied — must match by `property_id` intersection, not the created_at window which over-captures by 6; per the decision, the 423-member retry list is created only after production serves the merged fix).

**2026-06-02 trust reset:** Jarrad challenged the controller's Playwright-heavy verification and does not trust acceptance unless it is revalidated in Chrome/DevTools. Treat Playwright/CI/API/DB evidence as support only. Fresh revalidation so far: [[BMH Institute]] Chrome snapshot/screenshot `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-current.*` visibly shows `Lesson complete`, with separate Sandra outcome confirmation `/tmp/browser-revalidation-bmh-institute-outcome.json`; [[Closer Lab]] member Chrome snapshot/screenshot `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-member-recording.*` visibly shows recording `72ad25d8-1b09-4ef9-a278-82113c12ce75`, `100%`, transcript, and rubric `MET 5 / 5`, with separate Sandra outcome support `/tmp/browser-revalidation-closer-sandra-outcome-support.json`. [[Sandra]] production-readiness proof is GO on `https://sandra.bmhgroupkc.com`: real Sendillo production thread proof, `PR #236` sequence-admin gate, Chrome SOP matrix, and authenticated production non-admin sequence denial/enrollment behavior are all captured in [[Sandra - 2026-06-11]]. [[Jitter]] trust-reset browser work advanced in two steps: the earlier wrong-database/browser-auth mismatch was partially resolved by pinning production to the canonical `jitter-test` plane (`ypgntjjrrutjsratdwmk`) and proving controlled Chrome dialing in production, but that proof depended on a local scoped worker. Current blocker is no longer fixture creation; it is the **carrier swap**: Twilio is KYC-suspended/retired and **Telnyx is now the active carrier (account fully verified) — carrier validation PASSED 2026-06-04** — that carrier validation precedes the worker gate. The current Jitter gate (B2 plan, 2026-06-06) is **trust-boundary fix → browser-audio readiness contract → single-line live dial on Telnyx → Railway worker-backed unattended proof**. The downstream acceptance gap is still a real worker path, but only after the single-line Telnyx dial proof.

